# CI smoke run: boot → menus (keyboard) → Quick Race → drive a few seconds → pause → quit → menu,
# then exit. Exit 0 = every step ran and the UI stayed healthy; on a stuck step or a UI error the
# exit code is non-zero and the log names the step and the screen React showed:
#   cargo run -p recharged -- --user-data-dir <fresh dir> --input-script tools/scripts/smoke.script \
#     --exit-after 120
# Steps wait for the screen React reports (`wait screen`) instead of guessing how long a screen
# takes to appear (the first frames may stall while pipelines compile); the short delays only keep
# taps of one key apart (taps closer than 0.1 s merge). Format: docs/design/automation.md.

wait ui
wait screen title                  # the splash ends after its fade (on presented frames)
0.3 nav keyboardA confirm          # Title: any button
wait screen main
0.3 nav keyboardA down             # Quick Race
0.3 nav keyboardA confirm
wait screen trackSelect
0.3 nav keyboardA confirm          # the focused track: its Choose car button
0.3 nav keyboardA confirm          # → Car select
wait screen carSelect
0.3 nav keyboardA confirm          # race
wait racing
hold keyboardA throttle 1
@120 tap keyboardA item
@240 release keyboardA
0.2 tap keyboardA pause
wait screen pause
0.3 nav keyboardA down             # Restart
0.3 nav keyboardA down             # How to play
0.3 nav keyboardA down             # Settings
0.3 nav keyboardA down             # Quit race
0.3 nav keyboardA confirm          # dialog: Cancel focused
0.4 nav keyboardA left             # Quit
0.3 nav keyboardA confirm
wait menu
wait screen carSelect              # back where the race was started from
1.0 exit
